## Project-authored runtime data

Bounded matcher tables, alias rules, and suffix rules in `internal/nlp/` are
project-authored under the repository MIT License. They are compiled into the
library and are not populated by copying Natasha or OpenCorpora dictionaries.

## Test-only Go modules and external reference tooling

Indirect test modules (for example `github.com/stretchr/testify`) and external
Python reference packages (Natasha, Yargy, Pymorphy2, OpenCorpora wheels) are
documented in [docs/dependency-license-inventory.md](docs/dependency-license-inventory.md).
They are not production runtime dependencies; their dictionaries and wheels are
not embedded in the Go module.
